- For us to be like for first impressions,

00:07:33.270 --> 00:07:35.100
to say that you're more extroverted.

00:07:35.100 --> 00:07:37.620
But for me I was like,
"Oh, I got you guessing."

00:07:37.620 --> 00:07:39.224
- Yeah, no you definitely
caught me off guard.

00:07:39.224 --> 00:07:40.260
For sure.
- Okay.

00:07:40.260 --> 00:07:42.480
- So are we like happy with this lineup?

00:07:42.480 --> 00:07:43.313
- I don't know.

00:07:43.313 --> 00:07:44.910
I feel like Connor might
be trying to throw us off.

00:07:44.910 --> 00:07:46.080
I'm not sure, I've--

00:07:46.080 --> 00:07:46.937
- Which is why I think you should--

00:07:46.937 --> 00:07:48.352
(everyone laughing)

00:07:48.352 --> 00:07:49.185
- I don't know,

00:07:49.185 --> 00:07:51.030
but now I feel like I'm
overthinking everything.

00:07:51.030 --> 00:07:53.730
I guess I feel comfortable with
you guys staying like that.

00:07:53.730 --> 00:07:54.563
- Sure.

00:07:54.563 --> 00:07:56.100
- Yeah, do you feel like
you're the first one though?

00:07:56.100 --> 00:07:56.970
- Yes.

00:07:56.970 --> 00:07:57.890
- Okay.

00:07:57.890 --> 00:07:58.723
(Sierra laughing)

00:07:58.723 --> 00:08:00.390
Do you feel comfortable where you are?

00:08:00.390 --> 00:08:01.650
- Yes.

00:08:01.650 --> 00:08:03.300
- Do you feel comfortable where you are?

00:08:03.300 --> 00:08:04.920
- Yes, do you feel comfortable?

00:08:04.920 --> 00:08:06.003
(everyone laughing)

00:08:06.003 --> 00:08:08.880
- (laughs) My ego tells me
I need to be number one,

00:08:08.880 --> 00:08:10.830
but no, I don't think I'm number one.

00:08:10.830 --> 00:08:12.420
- I don't think I should be number one.

00:08:12.420 --> 00:08:13.937
- Ooh.
- Oh, okay.

00:08:13.937 --> 00:08:16.023
(Claire laughing)

00:08:16.023 --> 00:08:18.300
No, do you wanna switch?

00:08:18.300 --> 00:08:19.590
- Do you wanna switch?

00:08:19.590 --> 00:08:20.940
Do you wanna rock paper scissors?

00:08:20.940 --> 00:08:22.650
- If that's how you wanna solve that,

00:08:22.650 --> 00:08:23.760
we totally can but--

00:08:23.760 --> 00:08:24.593
- I don't know.

00:08:24.593 --> 00:08:26.760
- No, I'm comfortable in this
position right here, or there.

00:08:26.760 --> 00:08:28.080
I literally don't care.

00:08:28.080 --> 00:08:28.913
- Switch.

00:08:28.913 --> 00:08:29.746
- Okay.

00:08:29.746 --> 00:08:31.062
- Okay, confident, confident.

00:08:31.062 --> 00:08:33.000
We'll switch-a-roo.

00:08:33.000 --> 00:08:34.494
- Okay, so we think this is the--

00:08:34.494 --> 00:08:35.623
- This is the--

00:08:35.623 --> 00:08:36.456
- This is it?

00:08:36.456 --> 00:08:37.289
- Yes.

00:08:37.289 --> 00:08:39.872
(upbeat music)

00:08:41.262 --> 00:08:42.400
- [Interviewer] First off,

00:08:42.400 --> 00:08:45.993
let's have Gravity switch with Claire.

00:08:49.500 --> 00:08:52.323
Let's have Connor switch with Claire.

00:08:54.920 --> 00:08:58.331
And then, let's have
Sierra switch with Claire.

00:08:58.331 --> 00:08:59.164
- [Sierra] You were behind him.

00:09:00.420 --> 00:09:04.240
- [Man] This is most
introverted to most extroverted.

00:09:05.828 --> 00:09:06.661
(woman laughing)

00:09:06.661 --> 00:09:07.980
- Okay, so she lied to us.

00:09:07.980 --> 00:09:09.035
- Yeah I know.

00:09:09.035 --> 00:09:10.470
- I did not lie.

00:09:10.470 --> 00:09:12.636
- I wish I had more clue
about what was going on.

00:09:12.636 --> 00:09:13.610
(everyone laughing)

00:09:13.610 --> 00:09:14.700
- [Interviewer] Okay.

00:09:14.700 --> 00:09:18.780
- I did not expect Claire
to be most introverted.

00:09:18.780 --> 00:09:20.580
Especially because she kind of was like,

00:09:20.580 --> 00:09:22.290
guiding most of the conversations.

00:09:22.290 --> 00:09:24.540
- She just really seemed
extroverted to me.

00:09:24.540 --> 00:09:27.873
- My Myers-Briggs
personality type is ENTP.

00:09:27.873 --> 00:09:29.490
- I have ENTJ.

00:09:29.490 --> 00:09:31.191
- I have ENFJ.

00:09:31.191 --> 00:09:32.457
- I'm INFJ.

00:09:32.457 --> 00:09:34.438
- And I am INFP.

00:09:34.438 --> 00:09:37.605
(gentle upbeat music)

00:09:39.180 --> 00:09:41.130
So I did not lie (laughs).

00:09:41.130 --> 00:09:43.560
I come off very extroverted.

00:09:43.560 --> 00:09:45.750
I'm really capable of like
holding a conversation,

00:09:45.750 --> 00:09:47.370
and like talking to people.

00:09:47.370 --> 00:09:50.610
But like on the inside
I just get really tired.

00:09:50.610 --> 00:09:53.520
My anxiety just like holds me back a bit,

00:09:53.520 --> 00:09:55.620
just because of like
past events in my life.

00:09:55.620 --> 00:09:59.340
In college, I experienced a
pretty abusive relationship,

00:09:59.340 --> 00:10:03.270
that really kind of beat me
down and heightened my anxiety.

00:10:03.270 --> 00:10:05.100
I got like panic attacks and everything.

00:10:05.100 --> 00:10:08.220
And now I'm kind of scared
to go certain places,

00:10:08.220 --> 00:10:10.140
and just like to do certain things.

00:10:10.140 --> 00:10:12.660
So I think it's definitely impacted,

00:10:12.660 --> 00:10:14.490
just like how I navigate everything.

00:10:14.490 --> 00:10:17.100
Which sucks, but I'm
learning to come to terms,

00:10:17.100 --> 00:10:18.900
with like who I am now.

00:10:18.900 --> 00:10:20.340
- This is not what I expected.

00:10:20.340 --> 00:10:21.420
- Yeah.
- Like at all.

00:10:21.420 --> 00:10:25.470
- I like dress very colorful
to like express myself better.

00:10:25.470 --> 00:10:27.630
So that's like a big reason
why a lot of people think

00:10:27.630 --> 00:10:29.157
that like I'm super extroverted,

00:10:29.157 --> 00:10:31.650
and I like to be out
and going all the time.

00:10:31.650 --> 00:10:33.420
But this is just a way for me to like,

00:10:33.420 --> 00:10:35.160
another form of communication,

00:10:35.160 --> 00:10:38.190
when sometimes it's too
hard for me to do that.

00:10:38.190 --> 00:10:39.023
- When I first came in here,

00:10:39.023 --> 00:10:41.007
I thought for sure you were
gonna be all the way up here.

00:10:41.007 --> 00:10:41.840
(Claire laughing)

00:10:41.840 --> 00:10:43.830
So like, I just, I guess
it was just more of like,

00:10:43.830 --> 00:10:44.663
this sounds so corny,

00:10:44.663 --> 00:10:45.900
you can't judge a book by its cover.

00:10:45.900 --> 00:10:46.733
- Yeah.

00:10:46.733 --> 00:10:48.810
- But like that's
literally what we did here,

00:10:48.810 --> 00:10:51.090
and then turned out completely different.

00:10:51.090 --> 00:10:52.997
- [Interviewer] Do you like
to recharge with people

00:10:52.997 --> 00:10:53.830
or by yourself?

00:10:53.830 --> 00:10:54.663
- With people.

00:10:54.663 --> 00:10:55.860
- Takes me a long time to burn out.

00:10:55.860 --> 00:10:56.988
Let's just put it that way.

00:10:56.988 --> 00:10:59.477
- I have this answer prepared.

00:10:59.477 --> 00:11:01.920
I like to wear my comfiest leggings,

00:11:01.920 --> 00:11:03.300
my fuzzy socks,

00:11:03.300 --> 00:11:05.070
and I like to have a
pint of Ben and Jerry's,

00:11:05.070 --> 00:11:06.660
or cheesy popcorn,

00:11:06.660 --> 00:11:09.840
and either like watch
a movie or read a book.

00:11:09.840 --> 00:11:11.297
That's what I like to do (laughs).

